From f1937ecd93e7eb45bec73da359272994511e3758 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Schaka <jonastanzer@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] miopen: scope fused Winograd solver to genuine 3x3 on gfx803

ConvBinWinogradRxSFused wraps a legacy hand-written GCN3 assembly kernel
(conv_3x3_wheel_alpha_v9_2_7[_stride_2].s) that IsApplicable claims
generalizes to arbitrary filter sizes via Ceiling()-based padding, but the
kernel itself was only ever a true 3x3 Winograd transform.

Confirmed miscomputing on real gfx803 hardware (RX 470) against a real
audio-encoder graph (CLAP): a per-node ONNX bisection found this solver
selected for a plain 1x1 pointwise conv with cos(CPU_EP, ROCM_EP)=0.79-0.86
against a CPU-EP reference, cratering from 1.0 at every node before it. A
standalone MIOpen-only fusion-plan repro (no ORT, synthetic weights,
host-computed reference) reproduced the same systematic ~2% error for the
same 1x1 shape class in total isolation, confirming a real defect in the
padded-1x1 code path. Genuine 3x3/stride=1/group=1 shapes -- this kernel's
actual designed case -- compute correctly (cos=1.0000) through the same
kernel, so this is scoped to reject non-3x3 filters rather than disabling
the solver outright.

Fix: reject when the filter isn't genuinely 3x3, immediately after
y/x (GetWeightsHeight/Width) become available, before the Ceiling()-based
padding math that extends this kernel past its real 3x3 design.

Vendored into this experimental pipeline from
patches/miopen/winograd-fused-conv-miscompute.patch in ROCm-gfx803, which
carries the full investigation (including why no newer general-fused
Winograd solver exists to redirect to on gfx8) this commit message only
summarizes. Applies to MIOpen, gfx803 only -- this solver is dead code on
every other architecture already (see its own device-name gate).

NOT YET RE-VERIFIED under TheRock's own build against real gfx803
hardware.
---
diff --git a/projects/miopen/src/solver/conv_bin_winoRxS_fused.cpp b/projects/miopen/src/solver/conv_bin_winoRxS_fused.cpp
--- a/projects/miopen/src/solver/conv_bin_winoRxS_fused.cpp
+++ b/projects/miopen/src/solver/conv_bin_winoRxS_fused.cpp
@@ -76,6 +76,35 @@
     const auto K           = conv_problem.GetOutChannels();
     const auto y           = conv_problem.GetWeightsHeight();
     const auto x           = conv_problem.GetWeightsWidth();
+
+    // WINOGRAD_FUSED_CBA_MISCOMPUTE_PATCH: this solver wraps a legacy
+    // hand-written GCN3 assembly kernel (conv_3x3_wheel_alpha_v9_2_7[_stride_2].s,
+    // "miopenSp3AsmConvRxSU_CBA") whose Ceiling()-based padding below claims to
+    // generalize it to any filter size, but the kernel itself was only ever a
+    // true 3x3 Winograd transform. Confirmed on real gfx803 hardware (RX 470,
+    // ROCm 6.4.4) via CLAP's real audio-encoder graph: a per-node ONNX
+    // bisection (extracting each Conv's real input-to-output subgraph via
+    // onnx.utils.extract_model, so ConvActivationFusion still fires exactly
+    // like production) found this solver selected for a plain (group=1) 1x1
+    // pointwise conv (specialist.backbone.features.2.block.2.0, C=64 K=24
+    // R=S=1) with cos(CPU_EP, ROCM_EP)=0.79-0.86 against a CPU-EP reference,
+    // and a standalone MIOpen-only fusion-plan repro (no ORT, synthetic
+    // weights, host-computed reference) reproduced a systematic ~2% error
+    // (cos~0.98) for the same 1x1 shape class in total isolation -- a real
+    // defect in the padded-1x1 code path, not workspace reuse or session
+    // state. The same standalone repro confirmed a genuine 3x3/stride=1
+    // shape (this kernel's actual designed case, and what its own GetWti
+    // rates as by far its best) computes correctly (cos=1.0000, 3/3 runs),
+    // so this is scoped to exclude only the generalized (non-3x3) padding
+    // path rather than disabling the solver outright -- MIOpen's newer,
+    // properly-general Winograd family (Conv_Winograd_v13_3_12/v14_3_3, see
+    // solver/conv/conv_bin_winoRxS.cpp) already covers gfx803 correctly for
+    // arbitrary filter sizes on the non-fused path; this old kernel's fused
+    // (Conv+Bias+Activation) variant was apparently never carried forward to
+    // it. See winograd-fused-conv-miscompute.patch for the full writeup.
+    if(!(y == 3 && x == 3))
+        return false;
+
     const auto OH          = conv_problem.GetOutHeight();
     const auto OW          = conv_problem.GetOutWidth();
     const auto pad_h       = conv_problem.GetPadH();
